---
slug: test/mcp-invoke
method: post
format: json
---
{%- comment -%}
  TEST FIXTURE (gated): drives the in-process tool call (commands/execute/invoke) and the
  per-agent tool list (queries/registry/for_agent) for the identity of the request's
  bearer token, so tests/invoke.test.mjs can compare them with tools/call and tools/list
  for the same principal and agent. The token only identifies the caller here; invoke
  itself does no token, scope or rate-limit work. Body: { op: 'list' } or { op: 'call',
  name, arguments }. Served only when MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS is '1'/'true' (CI + eval
  hosts).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign test_gate = context.constants.MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS | default: ''
  unless test_gate == '1' or test_gate == 'true'
    response_status 404
    echo '{}'
    break
  endunless
  function auth = 'modules/mcp/commands/identity/resolve_principal', headers: context.headers
  unless auth.authenticated
    response_status 401
    echo '{"error":"unauthenticated"}'
    break
  endunless
  assign op = context.params.op | append: ''
  if op == 'list'
    function tools = 'modules/mcp/queries/registry/for_agent', principal: auth.principal, agent: auth.agent, delegation_mode: auth.delegation_mode
    assign out = { "tools": tools }
  else
    assign tool_name = context.params.name | append: ''
    function out = 'modules/mcp/commands/execute/invoke', tool_name: tool_name, arguments: context.params.arguments, principal: auth.principal, agent: auth.agent, delegation_mode: auth.delegation_mode
  endif
  print out | json
-%}
